## Building Rock Paper Scissors

### Defining Choices

```xiom
enum Choice {
  Rock;
  Paper;
  Scissors;
}

enum Result {
  Win;
  Lose;
  Draw;
}
```

### Determining the Winner

```xiom
fn play_round(player: Choice, computer: Choice) -> Result {
  if player == computer {
    return Result.Draw;
  };

  if player == Choice.Rock && computer == Choice.Scissors {
    return Result.Win;
  };
  if player == Choice.Paper && computer == Choice.Rock {
    return Result.Win;
  };
  if player == Choice.Scissors && computer == Choice.Paper {
    return Result.Win;
  };

  Result.Lose
}
```

### Computer Choice with Random

```xiom
fn computer_choice(seed: &mut Int) -> Choice {
  seed = (seed * 1103515245 + 12345) % 2147483648;
  let n = seed % 3;
  if n == 0 { return Choice.Rock; };
  if n == 1 { return Choice.Paper; };
  Choice.Scissors
}
```

### Full Match (Best of 5)

```xiom
fn play_match() {
  let mut player_score = 0;
  let mut computer_score = 0;
  let mut seed = 42;

  while player_score < 3 && computer_score < 3 {
    let player = Choice.Paper;
    let cpu = computer_choice(&mut seed);
    let result = play_round(player, cpu);

    match result {
      Result.Win => { player_score += 1; },
      Result.Lose => { computer_score += 1; },
      Result.Draw => { },
    };
  };

  io.println(player_score);
  io.println(computer_score);
}
```

